+// MapAnything parity contract: the map-anything-ggml reference runs on pristine
+// ggml CUDA numerics. The downstream precision overrides below (RMBG F32 GEMM
+// output on Ampere+, the SAM3 2x2/stride-2 conv_transpose cuBLAS fast path, the
+// cuBLAS route for F32 GEMMs that pristine ggml sends to MMF, the global
+// precise-math SiLU of sam3d_merged/0002) each perturb the result by ULPs that
+// the 24-block aggregator and the depth-confidence head amplify well past the
+// parity gate. The MapAnything graph builder names every matmul /
+// conv_transpose / SiLU output with this prefix so those nodes keep the
+// pristine kernel selection; every other task keeps the downstream defaults.
+static inline bool ggml_cuda_mapany_pristine_node(const char * name) {
+    return name != nullptr && strncmp(name, "mapany_", 7) == 0;
+}
